# Rate-loop tune from measured data (log 00000029, 2026-11-03 hover).
# Identified (airborne, 400 Hz RATE): K ~130 rad/s^2 per unit output on roll and pitch,
# total loop delay ~38 ms (motors/ESCs/props ~27 ms + the 20 Hz gyro filter ~11 ms).
# Gyro noise (3.2 kHz batch sampler): motor fundamental 60 Hz at hover, peaks 60/122/244 Hz.
# The 27 ms motor delay caps the rate crossover near 21 rad/s, so stiffness comes from the
# angle loop and the rate integral; less D (its high-frequency gain cost gain margin).
# Margins on the model: rate PM 56 deg, GM 6.3 dB; angle PM 59 deg; at K x1.25 PM 49, GM 4.3.
# Before: ATC_RAT_RLL/PIT_P 0.135, _I 0.135, _D 0.0036, _FLTD 10, ATC_ANG_RLL/PIT_P 4.5,
#         INS_GYRO_FILTER 20, INS_HNTCH_ENABLE 0 (FREQ 80, BW 40, REF 0, HMNCS 3)
ATC_RAT_RLL_P,0.15
ATC_RAT_PIT_P,0.15
ATC_RAT_RLL_I,0.45
ATC_RAT_PIT_I,0.45
ATC_RAT_RLL_D,0.002
ATC_RAT_PIT_D,0.002
ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTD,15
ATC_RAT_PIT_FLTD,15
ATC_ANG_RLL_P,9.0
ATC_ANG_PIT_P,9.0
INS_GYRO_FILTER,40
INS_HNTCH_ENABLE,1
INS_HNTCH_MODE,1
INS_HNTCH_FREQ,60
INS_HNTCH_BW,30
INS_HNTCH_ATT,40
INS_HNTCH_REF,0.275
INS_HNTCH_HMNCS,11
